Licensing of this repository
============================

This repository combines our own code with code from other projects.
The full license texts are in LICENSES/.

LICENSES/LicenseRef-RUB-SecEng.txt
    Copyright (c) 2026, Stef Halmans and Amit Kumar, Chair for Security
    Engineering, Ruhr-Universitaet Bochum. Applies to all files we wrote
    and to our changes in the c-fn-dsa files listed below:
        knobs.h, configs.mk, Makefile, eval_precision.c, test_ct.c,
        test_roundtrip.c, sha3_huang_cm4.s, shell.nix, shell-cm4.nix,
        fpr/ (except the files under the other two licenses below),
        scripts/, results/paper/, pqm4/crypto_sign/,
        pqm4/mupq/crypto_sign/fprbench.c, fprtest.c and signbench.c.

LICENSES/Unlicense.txt
    c-fn-dsa and c-fn-dsa-alt by Thomas Pornin (public domain). Applies to
    the c-fn-dsa files at the repository root, to sign_mq2.c and
    sign_mq2_cm4.s (from c-fn-dsa-alt), and to the binary64 code moved
    into fpr/ieee/ (all files there except fprtest_cref_ieee.c). Where we
    changed a c-fn-dsa file (codec.c, inner.h, kgen.c, kgen_inner.h,
    kgen_ntru.c, mq.c, sha3.c, sign.c, sign_core.c, sign_fpoly.c,
    sign_inner.h, sign_sampler.c, test_fndsa.c, test_sampler.c,
    test_sign.c, util.c), the original code stays under the Unlicense and
    our changes are under LicenseRef-RUB-SecEng; the unmodified originals
    are at https://github.com/pornin/c-fn-dsa (commit 3aa5048).

LICENSES/MIT-TWFalcon.txt
    Copyright 2025 NXP. The triple-word backend from TWFalcon
    (https://github.com/NXP-Research/TWFalcon): every file under fpr/tw/
    except fprtest_cref_tw.c. These files carry the NXP copyright notice.

pqm4/
    The vendored pqm4 framework keeps the licenses of its parts (pqm4 and
    mupq: Apache-2.0 or CC0-1.0, libopencm3: LGPL-3.0, CMSIS: Apache-2.0),
    stated in its files and in pqm4/libopencm3/COPYING.*. See pqm4/VENDORED.
